    'pdf',
    'The document "Getting Gender Right in Neural Machine Translation" is a research paper presented at the 2018 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing, aimed at scholars and practitioners in the fields of natural language processing, computational linguistics, and sociolinguistics. It provides insights into the challenges and methodologies related to gender representation in neural machine translation systems, making it a valuable resource for researchers looking to improve gender fairness in language technologies, as well as for developers seeking to implement more nuanced translation systems. This paper should be used as a reference for understanding the implications of gender in language processing and for guiding the development of gender-informed translation models.',
