    'pdf',
    'This document is a research paper presented at the 57th Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics, focusing on the evaluation of gender bias in machine translation (MT) systems. It is intended for researchers, practitioners, and developers in the fields of natural language processing and machine translation, providing methodologies and insights for assessing and mitigating gender bias in MT outputs. Users can apply the findings and evaluation protocols outlined in this paper to enhance the fairness and accuracy of their own MT systems or to inform further research in gender bias within NLP.',
